[48;2;223;239;233m[38;2;31;111;92m[1m Q1 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m You loved your brother, Marcus. He was the funny one, the one who drove a school bus for thirty years and never asked you for anything until 2019, when his wife Ruth needed surgery and he invested his whole pension in your fund. [0m

[48;2;223;239;233m[38;2;31;111;92m[1m Q1 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m You loved your daughter, Sophie, too. You paid her tuition, her wedding, the down payment on her condo — all of it from the same fund. [0m

[48;2;240;235;229m[38;2;168;55;27m[1m Q2 Q3 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m The fund was empty by 2016. You kept taking money in because admitting it meant admitting what you'd already spent: the house in Litchfield, the boat, the seat on the country club board, the version of Eliot Grant everyone toasted at the Christmas party. You moved new deposits into old withdrawals and called it a bridge. Every quarter you sent Marcus statements showing his money growing. You sent everyone statements. [0m

[48;2;246;237;214m[38;2;138;106;18m[1m Q3 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m The lie was one sentence: *It's for the family.* You said it to your wife Carol when she asked why you worked weekends. You said it to yourself at 3 a.m. in the study, moving numbers between accounts with your reading glasses on. [0m

[48;2;222;233;244m[38;2;44;90;138m[1m Q4 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m You want people to see a provider. A man who built something from a hardware-store father and put his whole family a rung up the ladder. When the investigators came, you told Sophie the government was confusing paperwork with crime. [0m

[48;2;247;223;238m[38;2;147;48;107m[1m Q5 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m The secret: Marcus called you in April 2021, before the collapse, because Ruth's cancer was back and he wanted to take money out. You told him the fund was locked for a restructuring. You took one more deposit from him that week — forty thousand dollars — and used it to make Sophie's mortgage payment. [0m

[48;2;247;227;220m[38;2;168;55;27m[1m Q2 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m The collapse came in October. Marcus lost everything. Ruth's treatment stopped in December. She died in March. [0m

[38;2;150;140;132m  Two years later, in your kitchen, you wrote a letter to Sophie and one to Marcus, then took the pills with whiskey. The last thing you did was check that the letters were still sealed.[0m


