[48;2;240;235;229m[38;2;31;111;92m[1m Q1 Q4 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m You loved your son, Marcus, more than the career that paid for him. You were the best anesthesiologist at St. Aidan's for nineteen years, and you said that sentence at every dinner party, adjusting it only slightly: "one of the best." [0m

[48;2;240;235;229m[38;2;168;55;27m[1m Q2 Q5 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m On March 3rd, you misread the dosage chart for a seven-year-old named Ben Calloway. He never woke up. You were the only person in the room who knew, and in the four minutes before the alarm, you changed the log. You entered the dosage you should have given. Then you told the review board that the pediatric nurse, Susan Whitfield, had drawn the syringe. [0m

