[48;2;247;227;220m[38;2;168;55;27m[1m Q2 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m Susan Whitfield lost her license in September. Her husband, David, left in January. You read her name in the paper twice that year and both times you made yourself finish your coffee before you allowed your hands to shake. [0m

[48;2;222;233;244m[38;2;44;90;138m[1m Q4 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m You wanted people to think you were meticulous. The colleague who checked her work three times. The woman who caught other people's errors. You were — after March 3rd, you were fanatical about it, and the residents whispered that Harper had saved more lives than anyone in the department. [0m

[48;2;246;237;214m[38;2;138;106;18m[1m Q3 [22m[38;2;36;31;27m Marcus lives in Chicago now. He still calls on Sundays. He believes you were exonerated, that the review board cleared you completely, and that the quiet in your voice when the case comes up is grief. [0m

